            <ArticleTitle>Beta-agonists and asthma: too much of a good thing?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>495-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In an unusual paradox, asthmatics who are chronically treated with bronchodilating beta-agonists sometimes experience a worsening of their condition. A new study describes one possible mechanism and reveals a potential new therapeutic target in the treatment of asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
